From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:56:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] feat(vk_native): declare the runtime's own X11 window
 full side by side

A plain OpenXR app runs in the runtime's own window, which is an X11
window (under X, or Xwayland on a Wayland desktop). When a display
processor's output is full side by side (XRT_DP_SCANOUT_FLAG_FULL_SIDE_BY_SIDE)
and the window manager announces version 3 or later of the X11 stereo
declaration on the root window (_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_SUPPORTED,
Stereo KWin), set _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT = 3 on that window. The
window manager keeps the window's place on screen and makes the X window
twice as wide, which can be seconds after it reads the property.

A Vulkan X11 swapchain is always the window's current size
(VK_KHR_xlib_surface / VK_KHR_xcb_surface: "it is only possible to create
a new swapchain on this platform with imageExtent being equal to the
current size of the window"), so the target becomes two views wide only
once the X window is: vk_full_sbs_refresh_locked now tells "declared"
from "presented", and the X11 window is presented both views wide when
the window helper has seen the doubling. Until then, and after a
withdrawal, it is presented at its own size.

While the window is declared, the window manager's synthetic
ConfigureNotify carries one view's width (the program's own units), so
the window helper takes the X window's size from the X server's
ConfigureNotify only, and knows the doubling from either the server's
width becoming twice the width at the declaration or the synthetic size
being half the X window's. comp_vk_native_xcb_full_sbs.h holds that
logic as a header; tests_comp_xcb_full_sbs pins it.

While doubled, comp_vk_native_window_xcb_get_dimensions answers one
view, so the window follow, the window metrics (the Kooima canvas) and a
legacy app's tiles see the window's place; only the swapchain and the
DP's canvas are two views wide. A legacy app's tile is half the target in
both cases. The X11 1:1 gate compares the X root with the panel's device
mode and reads no window size, so it is unchanged.

An app's own X11 window (XR_DXR_xlib_window_binding) and adopt-own-
window's child (#2322) are not declared; the FULL_SBS log line says why,
as it does for a window manager without the announcement.

